Subject: [PATCH] dstack-acpi-tables: offline ACPI dump for QEMU 10.2.1 (Canonical)

Provenance
==========
Derived from kvinwang/qemu-tdx@dbcec07c ("Dump ACPI tables", the QEMU_REV the
9.2.1 oracle built) and SCOPED to the offline, VM-less ACPI dump for building
`dstack-acpi-tables` from Canonical Ubuntu 26.04 `qemu 1:10.2.1+ds-1ubuntu3.1`
source (`apt-get source qemu`).

What was KEPT (all guarded by `#ifdef DUMP_ACPI_TABLES`):
  - hardcoded machine constants matching the dstack TD launch config:
      PM I/O base 0x600, sci_int 9, GPE0 = io+0x20, PCI holes
      (below_4g..0xfec00000 / 0x380000000000), MCFG base 0xe0000000
  - dump-and-exit in acpi_setup(): writes tables.table_data (== etc/acpi/tables)
    to stdout and exit(0). rsdp + table-loader are re-derived in Rust
    (dstack-mr/src/acpi.rs::build_tables), so only table_data is dumped.
  - hardware-bypass shims so the dump runs in a container with no TDX/GPU/vsock:
      vfio/pci.c early-return, vhost-vsock.c -> /dev/zero + skip init,
      hostmem.c skip mbind, physmem.c 20MB cap + anon RAM + guest_memfd guard,
      pc.c skip phys-bits check, x86-common.c instantiate 1 vCPU,
      acpi-common.c force MADT cpu entries enabled.

What was DROPPED vs the 9.2.1 patch (and WHY):
  - The `QEMU_ACPI_COMPAT_VER` / acpi_dump_compat_9_1() version-dispatch
    machinery (acpi-compat.c, the aml_pci_pdsm / build_link_dev /
    build_gsi_link_dev / build_iqcr_method / build_piix4_pci0_int compat
    rewrites, hw/i386/meson.build, tests/unit/test-acpi-compat.c). That path is
    only taken when QEMU_ACPI_COMPAT_VER < 9.2.0; a native 10.2.1 binary sets
    it to 10.2.1, so it is ALWAYS the "else" branch == native 10.2.1 behaviour.
    Verified: 10.2.1 acpi-build.c interrupt links already emit AML_LEVEL and
    acpi-common.c MADT already emits the Active-High/Level (0xd) xrupt override,
    i.e. exactly the compat "else" branch. So dropping it changes ZERO emitted
    bytes and makes QEMU_ACPI_COMPAT_VER inert (per the approved ADR).

Ports NEW for 10.2.1 (regions the 9.2.1 patch did not touch):
  - system/physmem.c guest_memfd: 10.2.1 REFACTORED the block — the old
    `assert(kvm_enabled())` became `if (!kvm_enabled()) { error_setg(...KVM
    required); goto out_free; }`, which would now hard-error under the KVM-less
    dump. Replacement: wrap the whole `if (flags & RAM_GUEST_MEMFD)` body in
    `#ifndef DUMP_ACPI_TABLES` (ACPI tables do not depend on the RAM backing).
  - target/i386/kvm/tdx.c tdx_cpu_instance_init(): 10.2.1 ADDED a hard check
    `if (xcc->model) { error_report("Named cpu model is not supported for TDX
    yet!"); exit(1); }`. The oracle deliberately uses `-cpu qemu64` (a CPU-model-
    independent placeholder — the ACPI tables do not depend on the CPU model,
    which is why the 9.2.1 oracle matches the `-cpu host` real host). The check
    is `#ifndef DUMP_ACPI_TABLES`-guarded so qemu64 is accepted for the dump;
    the following pmu/invtsc/force_cpuid_0x1f setup only touches CPU features,
    never the ACPI tables.

Constant re-validation (A1): the 5 hardcoded constants are unchanged from the
proven 9.2.1 oracle. 10.2.1's ICH9 PM model and q35 pciexbar property are
architecturally intact. MCFG base 0xe0000000 is dstack-config-specific
(!= q35 default 0xb0000000) and its correctness for 10.2.1 is confirmed by the
[H] RTMR0/MRTD byte-equality (Phase F), not offline.

Applies clean (fuzz=0) to `apt-get source qemu=1:10.2.1+ds-1ubuntu3.1`.
